---
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Story from '../components/napkin/Story.astro';
import AppShell from '../layouts/AppShell.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/base';
import { library } from '../lib/content';

const { cards, tracks } = await library();
const playgrounds = cards.filter((c) => c.data.griddle).length;
const quizzes = cards.reduce((n, c) => n + c.data.quiz.length, 0);
const flashcards = cards.reduce((n, c) => n + c.data.flashcards.length, 0);

const story = [
  {
    title: 'It started with breaking things',
    text: 'I started out as a tester who could also write code. Testing left me with a habit I never lost. When someone says "it just works", I want to know why it works, and what happens when it doesn’t.',
  },
  {
    title: 'C++, where every retry is real money',
    text: 'Then I learned C++ to work on payment gateways. In payments, a timeout or a duplicate request is somebody’s money. You learn to care about the boring details: retries, idempotency, and what happens when something fails halfway through.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Python, and the joy of simple',
    text: 'Next came Python, and I loved how simple it was. The code read almost like the idea itself. That stayed with me. If an explanation is right, it should feel that simple too.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Data science and system design',
    text: 'Then I learned data science and high-level design, and this is where I got frustrated. So much of it was folklore: rules repeated until they sounded like laws, huge diagrams that explained nothing, interview tricks with no reasons behind them. What finally made things click was a small drawing and one worked example. I still remember the relief.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Deep into AI',
    text: 'After that I went deep into AI, and today I work as a Senior Software Engineer specialising in AI. The topics kept getting harder, but the pattern held. The maths was rarely what stopped me. The missing picture was.',
  },
  {
    title: 'So I drew Napkin',
    text: 'Napkin is the notebook I wish I’d had at each of those stops. Every idea is drawn one stroke at a time, explained in plain words, checked against the facts, and practised until it sticks. If it saves the next person some of the confusion I went through, it has done its job.',
  },
];
---

<AppShell title="Why Napkin" active="about" description="The story behind Napkin: from tester to C++ payments to Python, data science, system design and AI.">
  <div class="container about">
    <header class="about__hero">
      <p class="about__kicker hand">the story behind the napkin</p>
      <h1>A hard idea usually clicked for me the moment someone <span class="hl">drew it</span>.</h1>
      <p class="about__lede">
        Engineers explain the important stuff on whatever is nearby: a whiteboard, a notebook, the back of a napkin at
        lunch. Napkin is that habit turned into an app. This is how it came to be.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div id="journey" class="about__story">
      <Story slug="about" diagram="journey" title="the road to Napkin" tldr="Tester, then C++ for payments, then Python, data science, system design and AI. This is why that road led to Napkin." story={story} trackRead={false} after="beliefs" />
    </div>

    <ol class="road" aria-label="The road so far">
      {
        [
          ['Tester', 'never accept “it just works”'],
          ['C++ · payments', 'every edge case is money'],
          ['Python', 'code that reads like the idea'],
          ['DS + HLD', 'pictures beat folklore'],
          ['AI · Sr. engineer', 'the hard part is the mental model'],
          ['Napkin', 'all of it, drawn simply'],
        ].map(([stop, lesson], i) => (
          <li class="road__stop" style={`--d:${i}`}>
            <span class="road__n mono">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <b>{stop}</b>
            <span>{lesson}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <section id="beliefs" class="beliefs" aria-labelledby="beliefs-h">
      <p class="eyebrow">What Napkin believes</p>
      <h2 id="beliefs-h">Keep it simple. Check the facts.</h2>
      <div class="beliefs__grid">
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="pen" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Draw it, don’t describe it</h3>
          <p>Every napkin starts with a picture that builds up scene by scene, so you watch the idea form instead of decoding a wall of text.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="check" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>No superstition</h3>
          <p>Claims get checked and numbers get computed. Every runnable Python example runs on each build and prints the numbers used in its worked example. Every napkin cites its sources.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="code" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Ideas first, any language</h3>
          <p>The explanations are language-agnostic: plain words, diagrams and pseudocode. Python only shows up in “Implement it”, because it reads like the idea.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="layers" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Learn it once, keep it</h3>
          <p>A quiz checks you actually understood; spaced-repetition flashcards bring each idea back right before you would forget it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="wifiOff" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Yours, and offline</h3>
          <p>No account, no ads, no tracking. Everything works on a plane, and your progress never leaves your device.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="belief card">
          <span class="belief__icon"><Icon name="sparkles" size={20} /></span>
          <h3>Built with what it teaches</h3>
          <p>The diagrams are code. The flashcards run on FSRS, a modern spaced-repetition algorithm backed by research. The whole thing is open source.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="numbers" aria-label="Napkin in numbers">
      <div><b class="mono">{cards.length}</b><span>napkins</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{tracks.length}</b><span>tracks</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{playgrounds}</b><span>playgrounds</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{quizzes}</b><span>quiz questions</span></div>
      <div><b class="mono">{flashcards}</b><span>flashcards</span></div>
    </section>
    <a class="made-link card" href={href('made/')}>
      <span class="made-link__icon"><Icon name="check" size={20} /></span>
      <span>
        <b>Almost 12 weeks of planning, building and checking went into this.</b>
        <span class="muted">See every source, how it was used and cleaned, and the algorithms inside.</span>
      </span>
      <Icon name="arrowRight" />
    </a>

    <section class="signoff card" aria-labelledby="signoff-h">
      <h2 id="signoff-h" class="hand">A note from me</h2>
      <p>
        Maybe you're preparing for an interview, or switching fields, or you're just tired of explanations that make simple
        things sound hard. I built this for you, and for the version of me who needed it at each of those stops. Start
        anywhere. Follow the drawing, check the numbers, and come back tomorrow to see how much stuck.
      </p>
      <p class="signoff__name">Rahul Tarigoppula<span>Senior Software Engineer, AI</span></p>
      <div class="signoff__cta">
        <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href={href('library/')}><Icon name="library" /> Open the library</a>
        <a class="btn btn--lg" href={href('made/')}><Icon name="check" /> How Napkin is made</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="https://github.com/RahulTarigoppula/self-learn-napkin" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="external" /> Source on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</AppShell>

<style>
  .made-link {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    transition: transform var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .made-link:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .made-link > span:nth-child(2) {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .made-link__icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--hl);
    color: var(--hl-ink);
  }
  .about {
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .about__hero {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  .about__kicker {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    transform: rotate(-1.2deg);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .about__hero h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5.4vw, 3.6rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  .hl {
    background: linear-gradient(transparent 58%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--hl) 80%, transparent) 58%);
  }
  .about__lede {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.22rem);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .road {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr));
  }
  .road__stop {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .road__stop:last-child {
    border-style: solid;
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .road__stop b {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }
  .road__stop span:last-child {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .road__n {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .beliefs {
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--topbar-h) + var(--safe-top) + 16px);
  }
  .beliefs h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-6);
  }
  .beliefs__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  }
  .belief {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-content: start;
  }
  .belief__icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }
  .belief h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  .belief p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .numbers {
    margin-top: var(--space-9);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(130px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .numbers div {
    display: grid;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .numbers b {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .numbers span {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .signoff {
    margin-top: var(--space-9);
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--space-6);
    max-width: 820px;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    background:
      radial-gradient(90% 120% at 100% 0%, var(--accent-soft), transparent 60%),
      var(--paper);
    transform: rotate(-0.4deg);
  }
  .signoff h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }
  .signoff p {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }
  .signoff__name {
    font-family: var(--font-hand);
    font-size: 1.4rem !important;
    display: grid;
  }
  .signoff__name span {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .signoff__cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
